{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"478f2e66d358ce26fb492819b10779f964ca0fcd2fe73ba04db72ec812a4bd51","digest":{"component_or_area":"CLI verb group registration and routing","key_entities":["rebar bridge fsck","rebar bridge check-access","rebar bridge setup","bridge-fsck","bridge-probe","jira-onboard","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","bridge_fsck.main","_bridge_probe","jira_onboard"],"problem_keywords":["CLI verb naming","command refactoring","backward compatibility","jira onboarding","bridge maintenance commands"],"propositions":["Three bridge maintenance verbs are being renamed to use noun-based spelling under a common `bridge` subcommand: `bridge-fsck` → `bridge fsck`, `bridge-probe` → `bridge check-access`, and `jira-onboard` → `bridge setup`, while maintaining old spellings as compatibility entrypoints","All three old verb spellings must remain callable and delegate to identical implementations without forking behavior, output schema, exit policy, or state effects","`bridge setup` passes remaining arguments to the unchanged onboarding wizard with entrypoint-specific `prog` parameter; the wizard's `--no-validate`, `--reset`, `--yes`, and URL/user/project options all remain supported","`bridge check-access` routes to the existing `_bridge_probe` implementation which performs Jira create/label/search/delete capability probe; it is registered as a distinct verb, not a flag on `fsck`, and `setup` calls it as final validation","Across CLI dispatch, schemas, help files, documentation, tests, CI workflows, and scripts, all references to old spellings must be migrated except in compatibility registrations, parity tests, release notes, archived docs, and ADR history","Both entrypoint shapes (`rebar bridge setup` and legacy `rebar jira-onboard`) coexist and share the same parser and wizard behavior while each displays its invoked command name in `--help` usage lines"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786708477301864001,"uuid":"e73d9c90-8186-4dec-9793-d47dab2a056e"}